@adaptive-mode-inference
Feature: Adaptive Mode Inference Engine
  As a user interacting with specialist agents via CLI, MCP, NATS, or voice through Jarvis
  I want the agent to infer which mode I need from the shape of my input and learn from my confirmations
  So that I don't need to remember flags or subcommands and the system becomes more natural over time

  Background:
    Given the specialist-agent harness has the ModeInferenceEngine loaded
    And the current role has a modes section in role.yaml defining available modes and inference signals
    And the Graphiti knowledge graph is available for mode learning

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP A: Key Examples — Core inference, confirmation, and learning cycle
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: The fundamental cycle — infer, confirm, proceed
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Agent infers mode from input shape and presents confirmation
    Given a role with modes "greenfield", "align", and "explore"
    And inference signals map "has_docs: required, has_codebase: absent" to "greenfield"
    And the user provides product docs but no codebase path
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent should infer "greenfield" as the most likely mode
    And the agent should present a confirmation: "I think you want greenfield mode — is that right?"
    And the session should wait for user confirmation before proceeding

  # Why: Explicit --mode flag must always override inference
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Explicit mode flag overrides inference and skips confirmation
    Given a role with modes "greenfield", "align", and "explore"
    And the user provides product docs with --mode align
    When the session starts
    Then the agent should use "align" mode without inference
    And no confirmation should be presented to the user
    And no Graphiti write-back should occur for mode learning

  # Why: Confirmation decisions must be written to Graphiti for learning
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Confirmed mode decision is written to Graphiti
    Given the agent has inferred "greenfield" mode and presented confirmation
    When the user confirms "yes"
    Then the confirmation should be written to Graphiti with the input pattern and confirmed mode
    And the Graphiti write-back should use group_id "role:{role_id}"
    And the session should proceed with greenfield mode

  # Why: User correction must override inference and also be learned
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: User corrects inferred mode and correction is learned
    Given the agent has inferred "greenfield" mode and presented confirmation
    When the user responds "no, I want explore mode"
    Then the session should proceed with "explore" mode
    And the correction should be written to Graphiti as the confirmed mode for this input pattern
    And future similar inputs should trend toward "explore" in inference

  # Why: The learning loop must eventually skip confirmation
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Agent skips confirmation when Graphiti confidence is high
    Given a role with mode "extract" and the user provides product docs only
    And Graphiti contains 5 or more prior confirmations of "extract" for this input pattern
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent should infer "extract" mode and proceed without confirmation
    And a log entry should note "mode inferred with high confidence, confirmation skipped"

  # Why: Must work across different roles with different mode vocabularies
  @key-example
  Scenario: Mode inference uses role-specific mode definitions
    Given the architect role defines modes "greenfield", "align", "explore"
    And the product-owner role defines modes "idea", "extract", "greenfield", "evolve", "impact", "scope"
    When an architect session starts with product docs and no codebase
    Then the agent should infer from the architect's mode definitions only
    And "extract" should NOT be a candidate because it is not in the architect's vocabulary

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP B: Boundary Conditions
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: Role with only one mode should skip inference entirely
  @boundary
  Scenario: Role with a single mode skips inference and confirmation
    Given a role with only one mode "generate"
    When the session starts
    Then the agent should use "generate" mode without inference
    And no confirmation should be presented

  # Why: Ambiguous input that matches multiple modes equally
  @boundary
  Scenario: Ambiguous input presents top candidates for user selection
    Given a role with modes "extract" and "evolve"
    And the user provides product docs and a build plan
    And inference signals match both "extract" and "evolve" with equal confidence
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent should present the top candidates: "This could be extract or evolve mode. Which do you want?"
    And the user's selection should be recorded to Graphiti

  # Why: No Graphiti history should fall back to pure signal matching
  @boundary
  Scenario: First-ever invocation with no Graphiti history uses signal matching only
    Given a role with defined inference signals
    And Graphiti contains no prior mode confirmations for this role
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then inference should use signal matching from role.yaml only
    And confirmation should always be presented regardless of signal match strength

  # Why: Graphiti unavailable should not block the session
  @boundary
  Scenario: Graphiti unavailable degrades gracefully to signal matching with confirmation
    Given the Graphiti knowledge graph is unreachable
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent should fall back to signal matching from role.yaml
    And confirmation should always be presented
    And a warning should be logged: "Graphiti unavailable — mode learning disabled for this session"

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP C: Negative Cases
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: Input that matches no mode at all
  @negative
  Scenario: Input matching no mode produces a clear error
    Given a role with modes requiring specific inputs
    And the user provides no docs, no codebase, no idea statement — only the role flag
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent should report that it cannot infer a mode from the provided input
    And the agent should list the available modes with their required inputs
    And the session should not proceed until the user specifies a mode or provides additional input

  # Why: Invalid --mode flag value
  @negative
  Scenario: Invalid mode flag value produces a clear error
    Given a role with modes "greenfield", "align", "explore"
    And the user provides --mode "build"
    When the session starts
    Then the session should fail with an error listing valid modes for this role
    And the error should not suggest inference as a fallback

  # Why: Mode inference must not silently pick a wrong mode
  @negative
  Scenario: Low-confidence inference always requires confirmation
    Given inference signals produce a best match with confidence below threshold
    When the session starts without an explicit --mode flag
    Then the agent must present confirmation regardless of Graphiti history
    And the confirmation message should indicate low confidence: "I'm not sure, but this might be X mode?"

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP D: Edge Cases
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: NATS invocation from fleet must support mode inference
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Mode inference works via NATS CommandPayload
    Given the agent is running in fleet mode via NATS adapter
    And a CommandPayload arrives without a mode field
    When the adapter processes the command
    Then mode inference should run against the command args
    And if confirmation is needed, a structured response should be published requesting confirmation
    And the calling agent should respond with mode selection before processing continues

  # Why: MCP invocation from Claude Desktop must support mode inference
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Mode inference works via MCP tool invocation
    Given the agent is running as an MCP server via Claude Desktop
    And a tool call arrives that maps to multiple possible modes
    When the MCP adapter processes the call
    Then mode inference should run against the tool parameters
    And confirmation should be presented as a structured response in the MCP conversation

  # Why: Voice interaction via Jarvis must produce natural confirmation prompts
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Confirmation prompt is natural language suitable for voice
    Given the agent receives input via Jarvis voice interface over NATS
    When mode inference produces a candidate
    Then the confirmation should be phrased as natural speech: "I think you want to explore these docs for features. Sound right?"
    And the confirmation should NOT use technical terms like "extract mode" or flag names

  # Why: Graphiti confidence threshold must be configurable per role
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Confidence threshold for skipping confirmation is configurable
    Given the architect role sets mode_inference.skip_confirmation_threshold to 5
    And the product-owner role sets mode_inference.skip_confirmation_threshold to 3
    When the architect has 4 prior confirmations for a pattern
    Then confirmation should still be presented for the architect
    And if the product-owner had 4 prior confirmations it would skip confirmation

  # Why: Mode learning must be scoped per role, not global
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Mode learning is scoped to role via Graphiti group_id
    Given the architect role has learned "greenfield" for input pattern "docs only"
    And the product-owner role has learned "extract" for input pattern "docs only"
    When a new architect session starts with docs only
    Then inference should propose "greenfield" based on architect-scoped learning
    And it should NOT be influenced by the product-owner's "extract" learning

  # Why: Subcommands (legacy CLI) should continue working as mode overrides
  @edge-case @regression
  Scenario: Legacy subcommands work as implicit mode flags
    Given the architect role supports subcommands "greenfield", "align", "explore"
    When the user runs "specialist-agent greenfield --role architect --docs ./product-docs"
    Then the session should use "greenfield" mode without inference
    And this should behave identically to "--mode greenfield"
